{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And to bring the first fruits of our ground</b> — like the omer and the two breads." "<b>Every fruit of a tree</b> — these are those mentioned in the verse: the vine, fig, and pomegranate, and the rest of the trees, and they are the seven species. And likewise the Sages said: one brings first fruits only from the seven species alone, as in the matter of \"and you shall take of the first of every fruit of the ground.\""], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:35.351169409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}